  "description": {
    "text": "The national finals after Battle Road Summer 2002, the only year they were held. In the junior and senior leagues' Best in Japan deciding match, in Hamamatsuchō, Tokyo, on 17 August 2002, each league's nine regional champions played a round robin for No. 1, 2 and 3 Trainer cards. The masters league's final, the Grand Master League, named its top four the Elite Four (四天王), and each got an Elite Four Trainer card with a photograph of the four in front of flames; from 2003 the title went to the top four of the Champion's League.",
